ASCII Tree Printer Test
=======================

1. Empty tree:
(empty tree)

2. Single node (50):
Red-Black Tree (r=red, b=black, R=red+dirty, B=black+dirty):
50(b)

3. Complete tree:
Red-Black Tree (r=red, b=black, R=red+dirty, B=black+dirty):
               50(b)
      /////////// \\\\\\\\
   30(B)                70(B)
   // \\\               // \\\
20(R)  40(R)         60(R)  80(R)

4. Same tree in DOT format:
digraph RBTree {
  rankdir=TB;
  node [shape=circle, fontcolor=white, fontsize=10];
  "1" [label="", style=filled, fontcolor=white, fillcolor=black];
  "1" -> "2";
  "2" [label="", style=filled, fontcolor=white, fillcolor=black];
  "2" -> "4";
  "4" [label="", style=filled, fontcolor=white, fillcolor=red];
  nil_8 [shape=point];
  "4" -> nil_8;
  nil_9 [shape=point];
  "4" -> nil_9;
  "2" -> "5";
  "5" [label="", style=filled, fontcolor=white, fillcolor=red];
  nil_10 [shape=point];
  "5" -> nil_10;
  nil_11 [shape=point];
  "5" -> nil_11;
  "1" -> "3";
  "3" [label="", style=filled, fontcolor=white, fillcolor=black];
  "3" -> "6";
  "6" [label="", style=filled, fontcolor=white, fillcolor=red];
  nil_12 [shape=point];
  "6" -> nil_12;
  nil_13 [shape=point];
  "6" -> nil_13;
  "3" -> "7";
  "7" [label="", style=filled, fontcolor=white, fillcolor=red];
  nil_14 [shape=point];
  "7" -> nil_14;
  nil_15 [shape=point];
  "7" -> nil_15;
}

